n{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})=3T(\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT(\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3T(\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299638 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}=-3\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}) & =T(-3\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =-3T(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =-3\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299639 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}=2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}) & =T(2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix})=2T(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2T(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]}
